  <section class="lang en" lang="en" dir="ltr">
    <p class="meta"><strong>Effective date:</strong> November 25, 2026</p>
    <p>Sakina respects your privacy. This policy explains how the Sakina app handles information when you use the app.</p>

    <h2>1. Information the App Uses</h2>
    <ul>
      <li><strong>Location:</strong> The app may request location permission to use your device location to calculate prayer times and determine the Qibla direction. Location is processed on your device. The app may store the last coordinates locally to make subsequent calculations easier. The app does not send these coordinates to the developer's servers.</li>
      <li><strong>Local app data:</strong> The app may store your preferences and theme settings, dhikr and tasbih statistics, Quran completion progress, and reminder schedules. This information is stored on your device.</li>
      <li><strong>Notifications:</strong> Notification permission is used to schedule local reminders, such as dhikr, prayer-time, and Quran-completion reminders, according to your settings.</li>
    </ul>

    <h2>2. Data Collection and Sharing</h2>
    <p>Based on the app's current design as described in this policy, Sakina does not create user accounts, send locally stored location, settings, or statistics to the developer, sell such data, or share it with external parties. The app currently contains no advertisements or advertising analytics/tracking tools.</p>

    <h2>3. Storage, Retention, and Deletion</h2>
    <p>The information described above is stored locally in the app's storage area on your device. It remains there until you clear the app's data or uninstall the app, subject to your device operating system's backup settings if enabled. You can manage location and notification permissions through your device settings.</p>

    <h2>4. Information Security</h2>
    <p>Local data is stored within the app storage area managed by the operating system. We recommend using a device screen lock and keeping your operating system up to date. No electronic storage or transmission method can be guaranteed to be completely secure.</p>

    <h2>5. Third-Party Services</h2>
    <p>Operating system and app-store services, such as Google Play and Android services, may be subject to their providers' own privacy policies. This policy does not mean that the developer can access information stored locally on your device.</p>

    <h2>6. Children's Privacy</h2>
    <p>The app does not require users to create an account or submit personal information to the developer to use its core features. If you have a concern about a child's privacy or app data, please contact the developer using the email below.</p>

    <h2>7. Changes to This Policy</h2>
    <p>This policy may be updated if the app's features or data practices change. The latest version will be published at the same policy page with an updated effective date.</p>

    <h2>8. Contact</h2>
